slug: registries-and-routine-outcome-data
title: Registries and Routine Outcome Data — Learning From Every Patient
area: Research & Evidence
level: Clinical
best: Third year onwards
minutes: 12
hook: Every day a clinic generates data that could answer big questions: who recovers, how long it takes and what helps. Most of it is lost in paper files. A registry turns routine care into evidence, and routine outcome measures turn each patient into part of a bigger story. || Har din clinic aisa data paida karta hai jo bade sawalon ka jawab de sakta hai: kaun theek hota hai, kitna waqt lagta hai aur kya madad karta hai. Zyada tar kaghazi files mein kho jata hai. Registry routine care ko saboot mein badalti hai, aur routine outcome measures har mareez ko bari kahani ka hissa banate hain.
goal: By the end, you'll explain what a patient registry is, choose a small set of routine outcomes, know the strengths and limits of registry data, and plan simple, ethical data collection in your own clinic. || End tak aap samjhayenge ke patient registry kya hai, routine outcomes ka chhota set chunenge, registry data ki khoobiyan aur hadein jaanenge, aur apne clinic mein saada, akhlaqi data collection plan karenge.

say: A **registry** is an organised system that collects uniform data on patients with a particular condition, treatment or exposure, to answer defined questions. **Routine outcome measurement** means recording the same few measures for every patient at set times, such as a pain and function score at the start, at discharge and at three months. Registry data show what happens in **real practice** with all kinds of patients, but without a comparison group, they are open to bias. || **Registry** ek munazzam nizam hai jo khaas halat, ilaaj ya exposure wale mareezon ka ek jaisa data jama karta hai taake tay shuda sawalon ka jawab de. **Routine outcome measurement** ka matlab har mareez ke liye tay waqton par wohi chand naap record karna hai, jaise shuru, discharge aur teen mahine par dard aur function ka score. Registry data **haqeeqi practice** mein har qism ke mareezon ke saath kya hota hai dikhata hai, lekin comparison group ke baghair bias ka shikar ho sakta hai.
analogy: Think of **a school record book**. A single child's marks tell you little. The whole school's records over years tell you which methods work, which classes need help and whether results improve. A registry is the record book of a clinic or a country. || **School ki report book** sochein. Ek bache ke number kam batate hain. Saalon ka poore school ka record batata hai kaun se tareeqe kaam karte hain, kin classon ko madad chahiye aur nateeje behtar ho rahe hain ya nahi. Registry clinic ya mulk ki report book hai.
compare: Strengths and limits of registry and routine data || Registry aur routine data ki khoobiyan aur hadein
head: Aspect || Pehlu ;; Strength || Khoobi ;; Limit || Had
row: Who is included || Kaun shamil hai ;; Real, varied patients, including older and complex ones usually excluded from trials || Haqeeqi, mukhtalif mareez, un buzurgon aur pechida mareezon samet jo aam taur par trials se bahar hote hain ;; Only people who reach the service, so some groups are missing || Sirf woh jo service tak pohanchte hain, isliye kuch group ghayab
row: Size and time || Size aur waqt ;; Large numbers and long follow-up at modest cost || Bade numbers aur lamba follow-up mamooli kharch par ;; Data may be incomplete or recorded inconsistently || Data adhoora ya be-qaida record ho sakta hai
row: Causation || Wajah ;; Good for describing outcomes, variation and rare harms || Nateeje, farq aur nadir nuqsan bayan karne ke liye achha ;; No randomisation, so cannot prove a treatment caused the result || Randomisation nahi, isliye sabit nahi kar sakta ke ilaaj ne nateeja diya
row: Quality improvement || Quality improvement ;; Lets clinics compare their results with others and spot gaps || Clinics ko apne nateeje doosron se milane aur kami dhoondhne deta hai ;; Needs case-mix adjustment, or comparisons can be unfair || Case-mix adjustment chahiye, warna muqabla na-munsifana ho sakta hai
steps: Starting routine outcomes in a clinic || Clinic mein routine outcomes shuru karna
step: Choose few, meaningful measures :: Pick two or three that matter to patients and are quick to complete, for example a pain score, a function score and one patient-chosen goal. || Chand, ba-maani naap chunein :: Do ya teen chunein jo mareezon ke liye ahem hon aur jaldi mukammal ho, masalan dard ka score, function ka score aur mareez ka chuna hua ek maqsad.
step: Fix when to collect :: For example at the first visit, at discharge and at three months. Make it part of the routine, not an extra. || Jama karne ka waqt tay karein :: Masalan pehli visit, discharge aur teen mahine par. Isay routine ka hissa banayein, aizafi nahi.
step: Record consistently and securely :: Use the same form or spreadsheet, a patient code instead of a name, and a safe place for the data. || Mustaqil aur mehfooz tareeqe se record karein :: Wohi form ya spreadsheet, naam ke bajaye mareez ka code, aur data ke liye mehfooz jagah istemal karein.
step: Look at the data regularly :: Review a summary every few months: average change, proportion improved beyond the MCID, and who is not improving. || Data ko baqaidgi se dekhein :: Har chand mahine khulasa dekhein: average tabdeeli, MCID se aage behtar hone wala hissa, aur kaun behtar nahi ho raha.
step: Act on it :: Use findings to improve care, share them with patients in plain language and report them honestly. || Us par amal karein :: Nateejon ko care behtar karne mein istemal karein, mareezon se saade alfaaz mein share karein aur imaandari se report karein.
check: A clinic records pain and function scores for every back pain patient at the start and at discharge, and finds average improvement. What can it NOT say? || Ek clinic har peeth dard ke mareez ka shuru aur discharge par dard aur function ka score record karta hai aur average behtari paata hai. Woh kya NAHI keh sakta?
ok: That the clinic's treatment caused the improvement, because there is no comparison group and many patients recover anyway || Ke clinic ke ilaaj ne behtari ki, kyunke comparison group nahi aur bohat se mareez waise bhi theek ho jate hain || Yes — routine data describe outcomes but cannot prove cause. || Haan — routine data nateeje bayan karte hain lekin wajah sabit nahi kar sakte.
no: How many patients improved || Kitne mareez behtar hue || Routine data can say that. || Routine data yeh keh sakta hai.
no: What the average starting score was || Average shuruaati score kya tha || Routine data can say that. || Routine data yeh keh sakta hai.
check: Why might comparing two clinics' registry results be unfair without adjustment? || Adjustment ke baghair do clinics ke registry nateeje milana na-munsifana kyun ho sakta hai?
ok: Their patients may differ in age, severity and other factors (case-mix), which affects outcomes regardless of care quality || Un ke mareez umar, shiddat aur doosre factors (case-mix) mein mukhtalif ho sakte hain, jo care ki quality se alag nateeje par asar karte hain || Yes — adjustment for case-mix makes comparisons fairer. || Haan — case-mix adjustment muqabla zyada munsifana banata hai.
no: One clinic always uses better scales || Ek clinic hamesha behtar scales istemal karta hai || Both should use the same measures. || Dono ko wohi naap istemal karne chahiye.
no: Registries do not allow comparisons || Registries muqabla allow nahi karti || They do, with adjustment. || Karti hain, adjustment ke saath.
check: Which is the best approach to consent and privacy for routine data? || Routine data ke liye razamandi aur nijiyat ka behtareen tareeqa kaun sa hai?
ok: Tell patients what is collected and why, use codes instead of names, store the data securely, and follow local rules for consent || Mareezon ko batayein kya jama ho raha hai aur kyun, naam ke bajaye codes istemal karein, data mehfooz rakhein aur razamandi ke muqami qaide follow karein || Yes — transparency and protection build trust. || Haan — shaffafiyat aur hifazat bharosa banati hai.
no: Collect everything in case it is useful later || Sab kuch jama karein kya pata baad mein kaam aaye || Collect only what you need. || Sirf wohi jama karein jo chahiye.
no: Share named records with anyone who asks || Naam wale records kisi ko bhi dein jo maange || That would break privacy. || Yeh nijiyat tod-ta hai.
mistake: **Collecting data nobody uses.** A registry that grows without anyone looking at it is a waste, and a burden for patients. Start small, make sure every item has a purpose, and look at results regularly. Another trap is cherry-picking: reporting only patients who completed follow-up flatters your results, so report how many were lost. || **Aisa data jama karna jo koi istemal na kare.** Registry jo kisi ke dekhe baghair barhti rahe zaya hai, aur mareezon par bojh. Chhote se shuru karein, yaqeeni banayein ke har item ka maqsad ho, aur nateeje baqaidgi se dekhein. Ek aur jaal chun-chun kar lena hai: sirf follow-up mukammal karne walay mareezon ki report aap ke nateejon ko achha dikhati hai, isliye batayein kitne chhoot gaye.
clinic: **Make it quick.** A two-minute questionnaire on a tablet or on paper, scored automatically, is more likely to become routine than a long form. Share the patient's own change on a simple graph, which can motivate them and open the conversation about goals. In Pakistan, a simple Urdu form and a locked cabinet or a password-protected spreadsheet are a sound start. || **Isay tez rakhein.** Tablet ya kaagaz par do minute ka questionnaire, khud-ba-khud score hota hua, lambe form se zyada routine ban-ne ka imkaan rakhta hai. Mareez ki apni tabdeeli saade graph par dikhayein, jo unhein hausla de sakti hai aur maqasid par baat shuru karti hai. Pakistan mein saada Urdu form aur taale wali almari ya password wali spreadsheet achha aaghaz hai.
reveal: Can a registry ever tell us whether a treatment works? || Kya registry kabhi bata sakti hai ke ilaaj kaam karta hai? || Registry data alone are limited, but some newer designs embed randomisation in a registry (registry-based randomised trials), which gives real-world data and fair comparison at lower cost. Registries are also excellent for spotting unusually good or bad results and rare harms that trials are too small to detect. || Sirf registry data mehdood hain, lekin kuch naye designs registry mein randomisation shamil karte hain (registry-based randomised trials), jo kam kharch par haqeeqi duniya ka data aur munsifana muqabla dete hain. Registries ghair mamooli taur par achhe ya bure nateeje aur nadir nuqsan pakadne ke liye bhi behtareen hain jinhein trials dhoondhne ke liye bohat chhote hote hain.
case: A group of physiotherapists in three cities start recording the same two-minute shoulder questionnaire and a goal rating at the first visit, at six weeks and at three months, using coded forms. || After a year, they see that patients with high baseline fear of movement improve less and are more often lost to follow-up. || The group adds a short conversation about fear and activity at the first visit, and tracks whether the results change over six months. || The next year's data show better improvement and fewer drop-outs in that group, and they present the findings at a national meeting.
safety: **Collect only what you need, and keep it safe.** Health data are sensitive. Limit who can see them, keep them off personal phones and shared drives, delete data when no longer needed and never use them for anything patients were not told about. Check the data-protection rules of your country and employer. || **Sirf jo chahiye jama karein, aur mehfooz rakhein.** Sehat ka data hassas hai. Dekhne walon ko mehdood karein, nijji phones aur shared drives se door rakhein, zaroorat na rahe to data mitayein aur usay aise kaam mein kabhi istemal na karein jis ke baare mein mareezon ko na bataya gaya ho. Apne mulk aur idare ke data protection qaide dekhein.
evidence: The AHRQ guide to patient registries describes registries as organised systems that use observational methods to collect uniform data to evaluate specified outcomes for a defined population, and discusses planning, data quality, ethics and uses such as describing natural history, measuring effectiveness and monitoring safety. A paper in the BMJ on patient-reported outcome measures in practice argued that routine collection can improve care when results are shared with clinicians and patients, but that systems must be simple and results actionable. || AHRQ ki patient registries ki rehnumai registries ko aise munazzam nizam batati hai jo observational tareeqon se ek jaisa data jama karte hain taake ek tay shuda aabadi ke tay shuda nateeje parakhe, aur plan, data ki quality, akhlaqiyat aur istemal jaise qudrati tareekh bayan karna, effectiveness naapna aur safety nigrani par baat karti hai. BMJ ke ek paper ne patient-reported outcome measures par daleel di ke routine jama karna care behtar kar sakta hai jab nateeje clinicians aur mareezon se share hon, lekin nizam saada aur nateeje amal ke qabil hone chahiyen.
memory: **Few, Same, Safe, Used.** Few measures, same each time, safely stored, and actually used. || **Chand, Wohi, Mehfooz, Istemal.** Chand naap, har baar wohi, mehfooz zakhira, aur sach mein istemal.
summary: Registries and routine outcomes show what happens in real practice, but without comparison groups they cannot prove cause. || Registries aur routine outcomes haqeeqi practice mein kya hota hai dikhate hain, lekin comparison groups ke baghair wajah sabit nahi kar sakte.
summary: Choose a few meaningful measures, collect them at set times, and compare clinics only after adjusting for case-mix. || Chand ba-maani naap chunein, tay waqton par jama karein, aur clinics ko sirf case-mix adjust karne ke baad milayein.
summary: Keep the data simple, secure and used, and report lost follow-up honestly. || Data saada, mehfooz aur istemal mein rakhein, aur chhootay follow-up ki imaandari se report karein.
card: What is a patient registry? || Patient registry kya hai? || An organised system collecting uniform data on patients with a condition or treatment. || Munazzam nizam jo kisi halat ya ilaaj wale mareezon ka ek jaisa data jama kare.
card: What is case-mix? || Case-mix kya hai? || The mix of patient age, severity and other factors that affects outcomes. || Umar, shiddat aur doosre factors ka mel jo nateejon par asar daalta hai.
card: Can routine data prove a treatment works? || Kya routine data sabit kar sakta hai ke ilaaj kaam karta hai? || No; there is no comparison group. || Nahi; comparison group nahi hota.
card: Why report loss to follow-up? || Follow-up ke chhootne ki report kyun? || Reporting only completers flatters the results. || Sirf mukammal karne walon ki report nateeje achhe dikhati hai.
deeper: Clinical audit and quality improvement || /learn/clinical-audit-and-quality-improvement || Using routine data to improve care. || Care behtar karne ke liye routine data ka istemal.
deeper: Outcome measures and minimal important change || /learn/outcome-measures-minimal-important-change || Choosing measures for routine use. || Routine istemal ke liye naap chunna.
source: Gliklich RE, Dreyer NA, Leavy MB, editors. Registries for evaluating patient outcomes: a user's guide. 3rd ed. Rockville (MD): Agency for Healthcare Research and Quality; 2014. || Registries for evaluating patient outcomes a user's guide Gliklich AHRQ
source: Nelson EC, Eftimovska E, Lind C, Hager A, Wasson JH, Lindblad S. Patient reported outcome measures in practice. BMJ 2015;350:g7818. || Patient reported outcome measures in practice Nelson BMJ
